From 08a18515bc913b58db9be1151a86b3c966705432 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:21:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] fix(#94): PlanResolution.file and the unwired adequacy
 benchmark are retired

The defect, verbatim from the issue: "a computed field no reader reads is invisible". Three OPEN fields:
`plan.PlanResolution.file`, `adequacy.AdequacyReport.abstain_reason`, `adequacy.FaultOutcome.family`.

PlanResolution.file: set at three construction sites, read by no renderer. The refusal's `detail` and the
assembly's `scope` already name the file, so the field is deleted (a negative test asserts it is gone and
the existing resolver test now reads the file from `assembly.scope`).

The adequacy benchmark: DELETED, not wired. `run_adequacy` has no production caller (ARCHITECTURE listed it
as "the benchmark entry point"), so the two report fields were read by nothing. The verb it would belong to
is `decompose`, but the benchmark works by writing an injected fault into the USER's target file, rerunning
the proof suite and restoring the file in a `finally`; an interrupted run leaves a faulted source, so handing
it to a person as a flag needs a redesign (an out-of-tree copy) that is a founder decision, not a field
fix. The module, its tests, the two generated goldens of its pure decisions (`adequacy_bucket`,
`bucket_is_finding`) and the ARCHITECTURE row are removed; the code is in git history at e730818 (#15).
Consequence recorded in the guard: `DecompositionApply.transform_class_id` was read only by
`run_adequacy`, so it is now a reflected-only field (it reaches `decompose --json`), and the pinned count
of those goes 36 -> 37 with the reason beside it.

Not closed: ExecutableProperty.{confidence, source_lenses} and TargetBinding.receiver_params (3 OPEN).

OPEN 5 -> 3. Disarmed, 3 of the 4 new/changed guard tests fail. Neighbour tests and guards pass under 3.14
and 3.12 apart from the unrelated `bound` entry; ruff clean under pinned 0.16.7.
